From: Christopher Stenger
Subject: h713: V2: a saved bootdelay cannot stop autoboot

`reboot bootloader` holds U-Boot's prompt: PREBOOT sees the RTC GP7 magic
and runs `setenv bootdelay -1`. That value lives in the environment, so
any save before the next reset stores it. A `saveenv` at the prompt does,
and so does typing `boot`, because bootmeth_rauc saves the environment
on every boot to count attempts. From then on every boot stops at the
prompt. On the sealed projector that is a board that never boots again;
on the bench it happened once (2026-11-20), after a saveenv made to set
BOOT_ORDER.

PREBOOT runs before autoboot reads bootdelay (main_loop():
run_preboot_environment_command() then bootdelay_process()), so start it
with `env default -f bootdelay`. A saved value is then overridden on
every boot and only the GP7 magic can hold the prompt for one boot.
bootdelay becomes a build-time setting (CONFIG_BOOTDELAY) on this board.

--- a/configs/hy200_qz713_v2_defconfig
+++ b/configs/hy200_qz713_v2_defconfig
@@ -34,7 +34,15 @@
 # No "usb start" either: U-Boot has no USB host on this board ("No USB
 # controllers found"), only the gadget for fastboot/UMS, and CMD_USB goes
 # with DISTRO_DEFAULTS.
-CONFIG_PREBOOT="if itest.l *0x0709011c == 0xfa57b007; then mw.l 0x0709011c 0; run fastboot_mode; elif itest.l *0x0709011c == 0xb007c0de; then mw.l 0x0709011c 0; setenv bootdelay -1; fi"
+# PREBOOT first restores bootdelay to its built-in value. `reboot bootloader`
+# holds the prompt with `setenv bootdelay -1`, and any environment save made
+# before the next reset stores that -1: a `saveenv` at the prompt, or typing
+# `boot`, because bootmeth_rauc saves the environment on every boot. Every
+# later boot would then stop at the prompt, which on a sealed projector is a
+# board that never boots again (it happened once, 2026-11-20). PREBOOT runs
+# before autoboot reads bootdelay, so resetting it here makes a saved value
+# harmless; bootdelay is a build-time setting on this board.
+CONFIG_PREBOOT="env default -f bootdelay; if itest.l *0x0709011c == 0xfa57b007; then mw.l 0x0709011c 0; run fastboot_mode; elif itest.l *0x0709011c == 0xb007c0de; then mw.l 0x0709011c 0; setenv bootdelay -1; fi"
 # A/B boot with Standard Boot's RAUC method (boot/bootmeth_rauc.c): slot A is
 # boot_a (p5) + root_a (p9), slot B is boot_b (p6) + root_b (p16). It takes
 # an attempt from the first slot in BOOT_ORDER with BOOT_<slot>_LEFT > 0, saves
